    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477-a1">

                <pb facs="0865" n="803" xml:id="pg803"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 120.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                            Silvela.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 27,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that I have this moment received a telegram from Washington directing
                    me to offer His Majesty Don Alfonso the congratulations of the President and
                    people of the United States on his providential escape from the dastardly
                    attempt of an assassin on Friday last.</p>
                <p>I need not say to your excellency how much pleasure it gives me to communicate
                    this expression of sympathy, nor how fully I share the sincere feeling by which
                    it was prompted.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to offer to your excellency a renewed assurance
                    of my most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
